body:
Hi {{first_name}},

Thank you for applying to {{university}}. We have now reviewed your application and on this occasion we are not able to offer you a place on the following course:

  Course        : {{course_name}}{{course_code_suffix}}
  Entry year    : {{entry_year}}
  Cycle         : {{cycle_year}}
  UCAS ID       : {{ucas_id}}

This decision will appear in UCAS Track shortly. UCAS rejections are common for popular courses and they don't reflect on you as a person — they reflect a single course's intake numbers in one cycle.

What to do next
---------------
  - Sign in to UCAS Track (track.ucas.com) so you can see the formal status.
  - Check the status of your other UCAS choices — many students hold offers from their other universities by this point in the cycle.
  - If you would like feedback on your application, you can request it from our admissions team at {{contact_email}}.
  - If none of your other choices come through, UCAS Extra and (later) Clearing give you further routes — your sixth-form careers and tutor team can walk you through both.

We wish you every success with the rest of your application and your studies.

The Admissions Team
{{university}}
